  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return grid\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find all 2s and group by column\n    col_twos = {}\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == 2:\n                if c not in col_twos:\n                    col_twos[c] = []\n                col_twos[c].append(r)\n    \n    # Identify the two vertical lines\n    line_info = []\n    for c, rs in col_twos.items():\n        if len(rs) >= 2:\n            line_info.append((c, min(rs), max(rs)))\n    \n    if len(line_info) != 2:\n        return grid\n    \n    # Sort by column to get left and right\n    line_info.sort()\n    left_col, left_min, left_max = line_info[0]\n    right_col, right_min, right_max = line_info[1]\n    \n    # Create a copy of the grid\n    result = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    # Find all 8s\n    eights = []\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == 8:\n                eights.append((r, c))\n    \n    # Process each 8\n    for r, c in eights:\n        # Check if this 8 aligns with the left line\n        if left_min <= r <= left_max:\n            # Draw from left line to 8\n            for col in range(left_col + 1, c):\n                result[r][col] = 8\n            result[r][c] = 4\n            \n            # Calculate corresponding row on right line\n            offset = r - left_min\n            target_r = right_min + offset\n            if 0 <= target_r < rows:\n                # Fill from left_col to right_col-1\n                for col in range(left_col, right_col):\n                    result[target_r][col] = 8\n        \n        # Check if this 8 aligns with the right line\n        elif right_min <= r <= right_max:\n            # Draw from right line to 8\n            for col in range(c + 1, right_col):\n                result[r][col] = 8\n            result[r][c] = 4\n            \n            # Calculate corresponding row on left line\n            offset = r - right_min\n            target_r = left_min + offset\n            if 0 <= target_r < rows:\n                # Fill from left_col+1 to right_col\n                for col in range(left_col + 1, right_col + 1):\n                    result[target_r][col] = 8\n    \n    return result\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return grid\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find all 2s and group by column\n    col_twos = {}\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == 2:\n                if c not in col_twos:\n                    col_twos[c] = []\n                col_twos[c].append(r)\n    \n    # Identify the two vertical lines\n    line_info = []\n    for c, rs in col_twos.items():\n        if len(rs) >= 2:\n            line_info.append((c, min(rs), max(rs)))\n    \n    if len(line_info) != 2:\n        return grid\n    \n    # Sort by column to get left and right\n    line_info.sort()\n    left_col, left_min, left_max = line_info[0]\n    right_col, right_min, right_max = line_info[1]\n    \n    # Create a copy of the grid\n    result = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    # Find all 8s\n    eights = []\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] == 8:\n                eights.append((r, c))\n    \n    # Process each 8\n    for r, c in eights:\n        # Check if this 8 aligns with the left line\n        if left_min <= r <= left_max:\n            # Draw from left line to 8\n            for col in range(left_col + 1, c):\n                result[r][col] = 8\n            result[r][c] = 4\n            \n            # Calculate corresponding row on right line\n            offset = r - left_min\n            target_r = right_min + offset\n            if 0 <= target_r < rows:\n                # Fill from left_col to right_col-1\n                for col in range(left_col, right_col):\n                    result[target_r][col] = 8\n        \n        # Check if this 8 aligns with the right line\n        elif right_min <= r <= right_max:\n            # Draw from right line to 8\n            for col in range(c + 1, right_col):\n                result[r][col] = 8\n            result[r][c] = 4\n            \n            # Calculate corresponding row on left line\n            offset = r - right_min\n            target_r = left_min + offset\n            if 0 <= target_r < rows:\n                # Fill from left_col+1 to right_col\n                for col in range(left_col + 1, right_col + 1):\n                    result[target_r][col] = 8\n    \n    return result",
